1
00:00:52,088 --> 00:00:55,108
[Episode 3. I've Never Been the Only One Naked]

2
00:01:06,173 --> 00:01:08,999
What's with this vibe?

3
00:01:09,574 --> 00:01:11,433
Don't tell me...

4
00:01:31,287 --> 00:01:34,589
Looks like the cramp's gone.

5
00:01:34,589 --> 00:01:37,178
You could've said something.

6
00:01:45,506 --> 00:01:49,201
That cramp went away fast.

7
00:01:50,384 --> 00:01:52,574
You're good at massages.

8
00:01:54,836 --> 00:01:58,392
Anyway, see you Monday.

9
00:01:58,392 --> 00:02:00,342
What are you talking about?

10
00:02:01,103 --> 00:02:03,683
We've got work to finish tomorrow.

11
00:02:05,733 --> 00:02:07,470
What a monster.

12
00:02:13,616 --> 00:02:15,281
See you tomorrow.

13
00:02:48,435 --> 00:02:50,653
Already? It's noon?

14
00:02:50,653 --> 00:02:53,878
No wonder I'm starving.

15
00:02:54,448 --> 00:02:56,784
Wait, that jerk...

16
00:02:56,784 --> 00:03:00,502
He made me come in, but he's not even here?

17
00:03:01,831 --> 00:03:03,542
Unbelievable.

18
00:03:05,292 --> 00:03:06,669
How much?

19
00:03:06,669 --> 00:03:08,671
Why is jajangmyeon so expensive?

20
00:03:08,671 --> 00:03:11,090
That's the going rate around here.

21
00:03:11,090 --> 00:03:14,789
With this rent, we have no choice.

22
00:03:15,302 --> 00:03:17,695
Business is slow enough as it is.

23
00:03:18,222 --> 00:03:20,683
Fair point.

24
00:03:20,683 --> 00:03:23,102
Then one order of jajangmyeon, please.

25
00:03:23,102 --> 00:03:25,396
We can't deliver just one.

26
00:03:25,396 --> 00:03:28,375
You need to meet the order minimum.

27
00:03:29,441 --> 00:03:32,069
How much is that?

28
00:03:32,069 --> 00:03:33,404
Twenty thousand won.

29
00:03:33,404 --> 00:03:34,989
Twenty...

30
00:03:34,989 --> 00:03:37,822
Twenty thousand won?

31
00:03:39,952 --> 00:03:42,121
Okay, I'll figure something out.

32
00:03:42,121 --> 00:03:43,812
Yeah.

33
00:03:49,169 --> 00:03:51,542
Should've brought cup noodles.

34
00:03:58,012 --> 00:03:59,838
Oh, my!

35
00:04:00,431 --> 00:04:02,057
You've been here?

36
00:04:02,057 --> 00:04:04,810
You could've told me!

37
00:04:04,810 --> 00:04:08,355
You expect your boss to report
to his secretary?

38
00:04:08,355 --> 00:04:10,983
Okay, maybe not.

39
00:04:11,859 --> 00:04:13,277
Had lunch yet?

40
00:04:13,277 --> 00:04:14,612
Let's eat together.

41
00:04:14,612 --> 00:04:15,952
I want jajangmyeon.

42
00:04:15,952 --> 00:04:19,325
I've never had a woman tell me
she wants jajangmyeon.

43
00:04:19,325 --> 00:04:21,160
Then we can eat separately.

44
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:23,329
Not going to meet me halfway, are you?

45
00:04:23,329 --> 00:04:25,748
You could meet me halfway.

46
00:04:25,748 --> 00:04:27,207
Then lunch is on me.

47
00:04:27,207 --> 00:04:29,710
I can afford a bowl of noodles myself.

48
00:04:29,710 --> 00:04:32,287
Yeah? Then you pay.

49
00:04:33,213 --> 00:04:36,133
Since when are you so modest about money?

50
00:04:36,133 --> 00:04:37,217
Deal!

51
00:04:37,217 --> 00:04:39,066
But...

52
00:04:39,066 --> 00:04:41,085
Does that place serve anything else?

53
00:04:41,085 --> 00:04:43,739
No. We're having jajangmyeon.

54
00:04:44,767 --> 00:04:46,533
Oh, hello!

55
00:04:46,533 --> 00:04:48,222
I just called a moment ago.

56
00:04:50,263 --> 00:04:52,127
Looks good.

57
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:58,967
See. Like this...

58
00:05:05,936 --> 00:05:07,822
This place knows its noodles.

59
00:05:10,225 --> 00:05:11,710
So good!

60
00:05:11,710 --> 00:05:14,243
Guess you get what you pay for.

61
00:05:16,083 --> 00:05:18,842
You'd never waste a bite,
even on your deathbed.

62
00:05:18,842 --> 00:05:20,776
You don't like jajangmyeon?

63
00:05:25,557 --> 00:05:26,892
Not really.

64
00:05:26,892 --> 00:05:29,353
How can anyone hate jajangmyeon?

65
00:05:29,353 --> 00:05:31,188
How can you eat it so happily?

66
00:05:31,188 --> 00:05:32,815
That's what baffles me.

67
00:05:32,815 --> 00:05:35,275
Oh, right. You don't have a favorite food?

68
00:05:35,275 --> 00:05:38,835
I said I've never thought about it.

69
00:05:41,323 --> 00:05:43,183
Come on.

70
00:05:43,183 --> 00:05:44,730
Eat up!

71
00:05:44,730 --> 00:05:47,121
I'm buying, so humor me.

72
00:05:47,121 --> 00:05:48,465
Here.

73
00:05:49,498 --> 00:05:53,210
Let me mix some in for you.

74
00:05:53,210 --> 00:05:54,425
There.

75
00:05:57,756 --> 00:05:59,216
What are you doing?

76
00:05:59,216 --> 00:06:01,176
With your used chopsticks?

77
00:06:01,176 --> 00:06:03,262
Seriously...

78
00:06:03,262 --> 00:06:04,471
Sorry.

79
00:06:04,471 --> 00:06:06,717
I'm so, so sorry.

80
00:06:09,476 --> 00:06:10,995
Give me your chopsticks.

81
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:18,160
Now, you have to eat it.

82
00:06:23,615 --> 00:06:25,075
Try it.

83
00:06:25,075 --> 00:06:26,201
Stop it.

84
00:06:26,201 --> 00:06:27,286
Come on, try it!

85
00:06:27,286 --> 00:06:28,495
I said stop.

86
00:06:28,495 --> 00:06:30,461
Just try it!

87
00:06:32,791 --> 00:06:34,491
Oh, no!

88
00:06:36,324 --> 00:06:37,504
Oh, no!

89
00:06:37,504 --> 00:06:39,423
What do I do?

90
00:06:39,423 --> 00:06:40,507
Seriously...

91
00:06:40,507 --> 00:06:42,482
Hold on!

92
00:06:42,482 --> 00:06:43,509
Wipes...

93
00:06:43,509 --> 00:06:44,876
Where are they?

94
00:06:44,876 --> 00:06:46,597
Oh, my gosh.

95
00:06:46,597 --> 00:06:49,343
Of course it's a white shirt...

96
00:06:53,479 --> 00:06:54,504
Oh, no.

97
00:06:54,504 --> 00:06:57,405
I can't believe this.

98
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:02,099
Well, you should've taken the bite!

99
00:07:02,099 --> 00:07:03,489
Oh, my...

100
00:07:03,489 --> 00:07:04,833
Hold still.

101
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:16,752
Wow, why is your chest so hard?

102
00:07:16,752 --> 00:07:19,658
You're just spreading the stain.

103
00:07:20,297 --> 00:07:21,716
Then...

104
00:07:22,382 --> 00:07:23,550
Take it off.

105
00:07:23,550 --> 00:07:25,345
I'll wash it for you.

106
00:07:25,345 --> 00:07:26,845
Forget it.

107
00:07:26,845 --> 00:07:28,581
Go buy me a new one.

108
00:07:28,581 --> 00:07:31,016
What's your favorite color?

109
00:07:31,016 --> 00:07:32,528
Why do you ask?

110
00:07:32,528 --> 00:07:34,312
You told me to buy a shirt.

111
00:07:34,312 --> 00:07:36,661
I need to know what color you like...

112
00:07:38,159 --> 00:07:41,151
Don't tell me you don't have one.

113
00:07:41,151 --> 00:07:42,495
Never thought about it.

114
00:07:42,495 --> 00:07:45,422
Seheon Department Store, sixth floor.
They'll know.

115
00:07:45,422 --> 00:07:48,075
So your tastes, even your favorite colors...

116
00:07:48,075 --> 00:07:51,209
You let other people choose for you?

117
00:07:53,914 --> 00:07:57,626
Stop asking and go get it. Now!

118
00:07:57,626 --> 00:07:59,506
Yes, sir.

119
00:08:01,213 --> 00:08:04,631
But they'll just give it to me, right?

120
00:08:04,631 --> 00:08:06,093
Yes. Just go.

121
00:08:06,093 --> 00:08:07,526
Understood.

122
00:08:13,527 --> 00:08:16,327
This is Mr. Kwon's usual brand.

123
00:08:19,064 --> 00:08:20,232
This one?

124
00:08:20,232 --> 00:08:21,772
Oh, yes.

125
00:08:23,026 --> 00:08:24,623
I'll get the same one ready.

126
00:08:24,623 --> 00:08:26,746
Okay. Thank you.

127
00:08:37,935 --> 00:08:39,993
That's expensive.

128
00:08:45,771 --> 00:08:47,812
Your shirt's here.

129
00:08:51,336 --> 00:08:53,107
Oh, my!

130
00:08:54,499 --> 00:08:57,420
I'll take it out for you.

131
00:09:07,321 --> 00:09:08,614
Oh, my...

132
00:09:08,614 --> 00:09:10,940
Just a moment, please.

133
00:09:12,297 --> 00:09:13,947
Here you go.

134
00:09:30,219 --> 00:09:32,873
What should I do with this one?

135
00:09:33,430 --> 00:09:34,904
Toss it.

136
00:09:35,904 --> 00:09:38,060
"Toss it?"

137
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:39,130
But...

138
00:09:39,130 --> 00:09:41,975
Does he know how much this costs?

139
00:09:41,975 --> 00:09:43,650
Unbelievable.

140
00:09:55,364 --> 00:09:57,704
So, you have an alternative?

141
00:09:57,704 --> 00:09:59,870
Yes, absolutely.

142
00:10:00,468 --> 00:10:04,390
Aimi writes her own songs.

143
00:10:04,390 --> 00:10:06,380
We can say she's working on new music

144
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:08,590
and keep her out of the press.

145
00:10:08,590 --> 00:10:12,010
As for New OX, they've been on a break.

146
00:10:12,010 --> 00:10:14,680
If we bring the full group back,

147
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:17,123
we'll get everyone talking,

148
00:10:17,123 --> 00:10:20,185
and that incident from last time

149
00:10:20,185 --> 00:10:22,442
will fade from the headlines.

150
00:10:22,442 --> 00:10:24,310
That's our proposal.

151
00:10:25,107 --> 00:10:26,483
So for this new single,

152
00:10:26,483 --> 00:10:29,326
we've gone all out on the group's return.

153
00:10:31,982 --> 00:10:33,321
Shall I call them?

154
00:10:33,321 --> 00:10:34,848
Come on in.

155
00:11:14,153 --> 00:11:16,310
Could you step out for a minute?

156
00:11:19,536 --> 00:11:21,913
These kids' futures are at stake.

157
00:11:21,913 --> 00:11:23,790
What about this company's future?

158
00:11:23,790 --> 00:11:26,293
And what about our KPIs?

159
00:11:26,293 --> 00:11:27,419
Forget the numbers.

160
00:11:27,419 --> 00:11:29,443
Give us a vision for this company.

161
00:11:29,443 --> 00:11:31,131
You don't like our idea?

162
00:11:31,131 --> 00:11:32,736
Then tell us why.

163
00:11:32,736 --> 00:11:34,589
Or give us a better one.

164
00:11:34,589 --> 00:11:35,954
Come on.

165
00:11:35,954 --> 00:11:37,155
What's with you?

166
00:11:37,155 --> 00:11:40,057
You know he's new to this idol business.

167
00:11:40,057 --> 00:11:43,036
Sir, if idol music isn't your area,

168
00:11:43,036 --> 00:11:46,083
maybe you should leave it to us.

169
00:11:46,083 --> 00:11:47,981
If you want my trust,

170
00:11:47,981 --> 00:11:51,109
bring me a strategy I can count on.

171
00:11:51,109 --> 00:11:54,537
I need a game changer to boost our KPIs.

172
00:11:54,537 --> 00:11:56,217
Bring me one.

173
00:11:59,632 --> 00:12:01,305
Sir...

174
00:12:02,122 --> 00:12:04,065
Oh, my gosh...

175
00:12:04,065 --> 00:12:06,126
By the way, what's a KPI?

176
00:12:06,126 --> 00:12:08,156
KPI, KPI...

177
00:12:10,530 --> 00:12:12,242
[Euneunhan Cleaners]

178
00:12:19,971 --> 00:12:21,367
What?

179
00:12:22,584 --> 00:12:24,393
What's in it?

180
00:12:24,393 --> 00:12:26,267
Oh, it's just...

181
00:12:26,803 --> 00:12:28,271
This one, right?

182
00:12:28,271 --> 00:12:29,564
This one.

183
00:12:29,564 --> 00:12:31,775
Why do you have a man's shirt?

184
00:12:31,775 --> 00:12:34,184
Whose shirt is this?

185
00:12:34,184 --> 00:12:35,697
I just found it somewhere.

186
00:12:35,697 --> 00:12:37,695
Found it?

187
00:12:37,695 --> 00:12:39,866
This fabric is top-notch.

188
00:12:39,866 --> 00:12:41,939
Smells nice, too...

189
00:12:42,967 --> 00:12:44,494
What's that smell?

190
00:12:44,494 --> 00:12:45,674
Jaja...

191
00:12:45,674 --> 00:12:47,278
That's it.

192
00:12:47,278 --> 00:12:49,167
Jajangmyeon!

193
00:12:49,167 --> 00:12:51,645
My nose never fails me.

194
00:12:53,266 --> 00:12:56,174
Oh, tomorrow's Sunday.

195
00:12:56,174 --> 00:12:57,975
Eun Chae.

196
00:12:57,975 --> 00:13:00,335
Let's get jajangmyeon tomorrow!

197
00:13:00,872 --> 00:13:02,472
Dad.

198
00:13:02,472 --> 00:13:04,308
I work tomorrow.

199
00:13:05,183 --> 00:13:06,989
On a Sunday?

200
00:13:07,702 --> 00:13:09,271
Well, look at my girl!

201
00:13:09,271 --> 00:13:11,357
Work must love you!

202
00:13:14,590 --> 00:13:16,190
Guess so.

203
00:13:17,529 --> 00:13:18,616
Good!

204
00:13:18,616 --> 00:13:20,907
I love it.

205
00:13:20,907 --> 00:13:23,118
Have some noodles before you go.

206
00:13:23,118 --> 00:13:24,536
Yeah.

207
00:13:24,536 --> 00:13:25,822
Okay!

208
00:13:52,716 --> 00:13:54,629
[Drop Your Dreams Here!]

209
00:14:01,364 --> 00:14:04,430
Wonder if they tossed ours, too...

210
00:14:27,724 --> 00:14:29,491
Come in.

211
00:14:36,183 --> 00:14:37,442
Yes.

212
00:14:37,442 --> 00:14:38,985
Get me antacids.

213
00:14:38,985 --> 00:14:41,112
Indigestion? What did you eat?

214
00:14:41,112 --> 00:14:42,706
Jajangmyeon.

215
00:14:42,706 --> 00:14:44,773
Jajangmyeon!

216
00:14:44,773 --> 00:14:47,160
That was hours ago!

217
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:48,411
See?

218
00:14:48,411 --> 00:14:50,524
You didn't enjoy it. That's why.

219
00:14:50,524 --> 00:14:52,317
Just get out.

220
00:14:53,116 --> 00:14:55,026
Hold on a second.

221
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:11,560
Why do you carry that around?

222
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:15,763
You never know when you'll need it.

223
00:15:15,763 --> 00:15:18,089
Give me your hand.

224
00:15:19,442 --> 00:15:20,826
Come on.

225
00:15:23,064 --> 00:15:27,644
Okay, let's get the blood flowing.

226
00:15:28,957 --> 00:15:30,557
There we go.

227
00:15:31,830 --> 00:15:33,835
Is all this touching necessary?

228
00:15:33,835 --> 00:15:38,877
I have to work it down
before I prick your finger.

229
00:15:45,215 --> 00:15:46,678
Does it hurt?

230
00:15:46,678 --> 00:15:48,836
Never had your finger pricked?

231
00:15:51,474 --> 00:15:53,101
It stings a little.

232
00:15:53,101 --> 00:15:56,896
The needle goes in about a centimeter.

233
00:15:56,896 --> 00:15:59,089
Why so deep?

234
00:15:59,089 --> 00:16:00,191
Scared?

235
00:16:00,191 --> 00:16:02,402
Close your eyes if you are.

236
00:16:02,402 --> 00:16:03,724
No.

237
00:16:03,724 --> 00:16:05,337
Forget it.

238
00:16:06,027 --> 00:16:07,949
Here comes the pinch.

239
00:16:07,949 --> 00:16:09,684
Wait!

240
00:16:11,494 --> 00:16:13,121
You're doing it right now?

241
00:16:13,121 --> 00:16:15,990
On three, okay?

242
00:16:15,990 --> 00:16:17,582
- Three?
- Yes.

243
00:16:17,582 --> 00:16:18,914
Three...

244
00:16:19,711 --> 00:16:22,294
One, two, three!

245
00:16:24,990 --> 00:16:26,801
Kidding.

246
00:16:26,801 --> 00:16:28,852
For real this time.

247
00:16:30,204 --> 00:16:31,570
One...

248
00:16:31,570 --> 00:16:32,850
Oh, my!

249
00:16:32,850 --> 00:16:34,017
Three! Three!

250
00:16:34,017 --> 00:16:35,226
That was one!

251
00:16:35,226 --> 00:16:37,100
Look. You really are sick.

252
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:38,980
Look at that dark blood.

253
00:16:38,980 --> 00:16:40,273
Oh, no.

254
00:16:40,273 --> 00:16:42,263
That must've hurt.

255
00:16:43,346 --> 00:16:44,886
All right.

256
00:16:45,670 --> 00:16:48,405
Now let's get a good burp out of you.

257
00:16:48,405 --> 00:16:50,367
That's enough.

258
00:16:50,367 --> 00:16:52,892
Don't be shy!

259
00:16:52,892 --> 00:16:54,238
Stop pounding my back.

260
00:16:54,238 --> 00:16:55,747
It hurts.

261
00:16:55,747 --> 00:16:57,524
Oh, it hurts?

262
00:17:01,503 --> 00:17:05,272
So... what song have you had on all day?

263
00:17:05,272 --> 00:17:07,213
It's our new single.

264
00:17:07,213 --> 00:17:08,512
I can't stand it.

265
00:17:08,512 --> 00:17:09,617
Why not?

266
00:17:09,617 --> 00:17:13,193
I don't listen to music with vocals.

267
00:17:13,193 --> 00:17:14,224
Why?

268
00:17:14,224 --> 00:17:16,292
Too noisy.

269
00:17:19,438 --> 00:17:21,889
Well, fair enough.

270
00:17:21,889 --> 00:17:24,859
Music's a matter of taste.

271
00:17:24,859 --> 00:17:26,778
But I think...

272
00:17:26,778 --> 00:17:29,350
music isn't about genre.

273
00:17:29,350 --> 00:17:31,551
It's about the world an artist creates.

274
00:17:31,551 --> 00:17:35,122
Whether it's a song or an instrumental.

275
00:17:35,122 --> 00:17:36,962
Their own world?

276
00:17:37,947 --> 00:17:40,600
What does music mean to you?

277
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:41,835
To me,

278
00:17:41,835 --> 00:17:46,005
music connects people across time and space.

279
00:17:46,005 --> 00:17:48,751
And it brings comfort.

280
00:17:48,751 --> 00:17:50,392
I don't know about that.

281
00:17:52,612 --> 00:17:54,848
Think about birthdays.

282
00:17:54,848 --> 00:17:56,558
When the people you love

283
00:17:56,558 --> 00:17:59,272
sing Happy Birthday to you,

284
00:17:59,272 --> 00:18:01,830
it makes you feel great, right?

285
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:06,818
When my mom finished singing Happy Birthday,

286
00:18:06,818 --> 00:18:10,645
she'd sprinkle magic dust on the cake.

287
00:18:10,645 --> 00:18:14,264
She'd tell me to make a wish.

288
00:18:15,660 --> 00:18:17,452
Enough. Get out.

289
00:18:17,452 --> 00:18:18,480
Did you burp?

290
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:21,624
I'm not going to. Drop it.

291
00:18:21,624 --> 00:18:23,140
Okay.

292
00:18:30,633 --> 00:18:33,011
When the people you love

293
00:18:33,011 --> 00:18:35,305
sing Happy Birthday to you,

294
00:18:35,305 --> 00:18:37,651
it makes you feel great, right?

295
00:18:43,396 --> 00:18:51,029
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

296
00:18:51,029 --> 00:18:55,040
♪ Dear my Do Hyeok ♪

297
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:58,726
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

298
00:19:01,956 --> 00:19:05,126
Making someone happy...

299
00:19:44,249 --> 00:19:46,167
Did you burp?

300
00:19:46,167 --> 00:19:49,671
I told you to drop it.

301
00:19:49,671 --> 00:19:53,550
And if you keep playing that music,
you can go home.

302
00:19:53,550 --> 00:19:55,194
Really?

303
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:58,225
I should've played music hours ago!

304
00:19:58,225 --> 00:20:00,842
I mean stop playing it from now on.

305
00:20:02,767 --> 00:20:06,152
Those albums left in the lobby...

306
00:20:06,152 --> 00:20:07,707
Never listened to these?

307
00:20:07,707 --> 00:20:10,108
They worked so hard on them.

308
00:20:10,108 --> 00:20:12,261
You didn't even listen? That's harsh.

309
00:20:12,261 --> 00:20:14,279
They're not worth it.

310
00:20:14,279 --> 00:20:16,865
Music means different things to everyone.

311
00:20:16,865 --> 00:20:19,117
Give them a listen sometime.

312
00:20:19,117 --> 00:20:21,828
Every artist has a world to share.

313
00:20:21,828 --> 00:20:22,945
Enough.

314
00:20:22,945 --> 00:20:24,581
Let's get dinner.

315
00:20:24,581 --> 00:20:25,940
Out of nowhere?

316
00:20:25,940 --> 00:20:28,118
This time, I choose the food.

317
00:20:30,422 --> 00:20:35,222
Rich people love the view from up high.

318
00:20:35,222 --> 00:20:38,373
I prefer the ground floor,
where I can see everyone.

319
00:20:43,141 --> 00:20:45,226
You like all kinds of meat?

320
00:20:45,226 --> 00:20:46,267
Sure.

321
00:20:46,267 --> 00:20:48,447
I'll even eat the bones.

322
00:20:49,414 --> 00:20:52,358
I'll treat you to pig's feet next time.

323
00:20:52,358 --> 00:20:54,235
They're really expensive, you know.

324
00:20:54,235 --> 00:20:56,635
I'll definitely pass.

325
00:21:05,496 --> 00:21:07,498
Let's start with ceviche,

326
00:21:07,498 --> 00:21:10,752
ravioli parmigiana, and en casserole.

327
00:21:10,752 --> 00:21:14,380
And chateaubriand for the steak.

328
00:21:14,380 --> 00:21:15,566
And the wine?

329
00:21:15,566 --> 00:21:18,145
Your Château Margaux is ready, sir.

330
00:21:18,145 --> 00:21:19,307
Oh, yeah.

331
00:21:25,225 --> 00:21:28,811
Even the menu sounds boring.

332
00:21:28,811 --> 00:21:32,315
Perhaps it's beyond your palate.

333
00:21:32,315 --> 00:21:34,484
And you?

334
00:21:34,484 --> 00:21:37,320
Are you even enjoying yourself?

335
00:21:37,320 --> 00:21:40,177
Never thought about it.

336
00:21:51,579 --> 00:21:53,960
Oh, this is good.

337
00:21:56,968 --> 00:21:58,693
Kwon Do Hyeok?

338
00:21:58,693 --> 00:22:00,628
Hey, Do Hyeok!

339
00:22:04,138 --> 00:22:05,932
Long time no see!

340
00:22:05,932 --> 00:22:07,433
Heard you went bankrupt.

341
00:22:07,433 --> 00:22:09,352
Is that why you came back to Korea?

342
00:22:09,352 --> 00:22:11,197
Just keep walking.

343
00:22:11,197 --> 00:22:13,982
I'm staying right here.

344
00:22:13,982 --> 00:22:16,228
Then get back to it.

345
00:22:16,228 --> 00:22:18,194
Still as prickly as ever.

346
00:22:18,194 --> 00:22:20,368
Because you're on a date?

347
00:22:22,942 --> 00:22:26,282
Your taste sure has changed.

348
00:22:27,954 --> 00:22:31,327
Who's this Tinky Winky?

349
00:22:41,092 --> 00:22:43,011
What did she just call me?

350
00:22:43,011 --> 00:22:45,555
You're interrupting. Get lost.

351
00:22:45,555 --> 00:22:47,161
Tinky Winky.

352
00:22:48,646 --> 00:22:51,275
I'll be on my way.

353
00:22:52,903 --> 00:22:54,856
Arrogant prick.

354
00:22:58,109 --> 00:23:01,249
You do have friends, right?

355
00:23:03,870 --> 00:23:05,022
You.

356
00:23:05,022 --> 00:23:07,742
Oh, guess not.

357
00:23:08,694 --> 00:23:11,216
What's your definition of a friend?

358
00:23:13,291 --> 00:23:16,669
Someone I can eat anything with and feel fine.

359
00:23:16,669 --> 00:23:18,755
You never get sick eating with me,

360
00:23:18,755 --> 00:23:21,291
so I must be your friend.

361
00:23:22,550 --> 00:23:25,261
With that little emotional intelligence,

362
00:23:25,261 --> 00:23:28,455
how did you dare make that bet?

363
00:23:28,455 --> 00:23:30,808
If you think a fancy dinner

364
00:23:30,808 --> 00:23:33,644
will make me fall for you,

365
00:23:33,644 --> 00:23:36,314
forget it.

366
00:23:36,314 --> 00:23:40,340
I'm winning this bet.

367
00:23:49,327 --> 00:23:50,861
This is the life.

368
00:24:01,798 --> 00:24:04,639
Too much wine will get you drunk.

369
00:24:06,094 --> 00:24:08,846
No matter how much I drink,

370
00:24:08,846 --> 00:24:12,266
I always make it home.

371
00:24:12,266 --> 00:24:14,632
Even if you have to crawl?

372
00:24:15,238 --> 00:24:16,859
Exactly.

373
00:24:18,732 --> 00:24:20,439
Another bottle?

374
00:24:26,377 --> 00:24:28,144
I love this.

375
00:24:53,783 --> 00:25:01,566
♪ The sky's so beautiful ♪

376
00:25:01,566 --> 00:25:03,151
Don't sing.

377
00:25:03,151 --> 00:25:09,699
♪ Like a violet-colored dream ♪

378
00:25:11,387 --> 00:25:13,369
- ♪ That sky... ♪
- That's enough.

379
00:25:13,369 --> 00:25:14,603
Time to go.

380
00:25:14,603 --> 00:25:20,126
♪ Like a violet-colored dream ♪

381
00:25:20,126 --> 00:25:22,963
♪ Oh, that sky above... ♪

382
00:25:23,838 --> 00:25:26,632
♪ I hope it's not a dream ♪

383
00:25:26,632 --> 00:25:28,050
If you don't get up now,

384
00:25:28,050 --> 00:25:30,576
you're paying the whole bill.

385
00:25:30,576 --> 00:25:32,221
Oh, no!

386
00:25:32,221 --> 00:25:34,724
I'm broke!

387
00:25:34,724 --> 00:25:39,103
I've only got 20,000 won to my name.

388
00:25:39,103 --> 00:25:43,941
I can't even afford pig's feet.

389
00:25:43,941 --> 00:25:46,319
What about the ten million I gave you?

390
00:25:46,319 --> 00:25:48,154
You spent it already?

391
00:25:48,154 --> 00:25:50,698
Oh, that?

392
00:25:50,698 --> 00:25:56,098
I threw it in that sleazy manager's face.

393
00:25:56,098 --> 00:25:58,122
Take this and get lost!

394
00:25:58,122 --> 00:26:02,188
You two-bit creep!

395
00:26:06,672 --> 00:26:11,886
♪ The sky's so beautiful ♪

396
00:26:11,886 --> 00:26:16,563
♪ The sky has abandoned me ♪

397
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:19,268
Wait.

398
00:26:19,268 --> 00:26:20,994
Where are we off to?

399
00:26:22,063 --> 00:26:25,441
♪ People say... ♪

400
00:26:25,441 --> 00:26:28,361
♪ Will you settle down? ♪

401
00:26:28,361 --> 00:26:31,364
♪ My gestures are a question mark ♪

402
00:26:31,364 --> 00:26:35,076
♪ Maybe I left my mind behind ♪

403
00:26:35,076 --> 00:26:36,786
Lee Eun Chae!

404
00:26:36,786 --> 00:26:39,664
I'll get you a cab.

405
00:26:39,664 --> 00:26:42,250
♪ Pretending I'm normal... ♪

406
00:26:42,250 --> 00:26:43,417
Lee Eun...

407
00:26:43,417 --> 00:26:45,366
You said you could crawl home!

408
00:26:45,366 --> 00:26:47,699
How are you getting there?

409
00:26:49,090 --> 00:26:52,952
♪ I'll fly like a butterfly ♪

410
00:26:52,952 --> 00:26:54,679
Beats me.

411
00:26:54,679 --> 00:26:56,465
Driver's coming.

412
00:27:05,231 --> 00:27:07,775
Farewell, everyone!

413
00:27:07,775 --> 00:27:10,871
I'm leaving this miserable world behind!

414
00:27:10,871 --> 00:27:12,530
Hey! Where are you going?

415
00:27:12,530 --> 00:27:14,418
I called a driver!

416
00:27:14,418 --> 00:27:17,036
My house!

417
00:27:17,036 --> 00:27:18,578
You're running?

418
00:27:18,578 --> 00:27:20,418
For God's sake...

419
00:27:26,093 --> 00:27:28,083
Where am I?

420
00:27:28,083 --> 00:27:30,106
Is this my house?

421
00:27:40,185 --> 00:27:41,642
Hey! Don't run...

422
00:27:41,642 --> 00:27:42,685
Jeez.

423
00:27:42,685 --> 00:27:44,410
Stop running!

424
00:27:53,472 --> 00:27:54,642
Hey...

425
00:27:55,321 --> 00:27:57,262
Oh, that's me!

426
00:28:00,786 --> 00:28:02,540
Where am I?

427
00:28:32,485 --> 00:28:34,846
I feel sick.

428
00:28:37,245 --> 00:28:39,409
Lee Eun Chae.

429
00:28:39,409 --> 00:28:41,786
Lee Eun Chae, wake up.

430
00:28:41,786 --> 00:28:43,526
Get up.

431
00:28:48,793 --> 00:28:52,254
Thank you, driver.

432
00:28:52,254 --> 00:28:53,756
Oh, right.

433
00:28:53,756 --> 00:28:55,852
One second.

434
00:28:57,144 --> 00:28:59,553
Here it is.

435
00:28:59,553 --> 00:29:02,531
Here you go, sir.

436
00:29:09,315 --> 00:29:11,075
Ma'am.

437
00:29:11,575 --> 00:29:14,109
That's 14,000 won.

438
00:29:14,860 --> 00:29:17,780
Oh, really?

439
00:29:17,780 --> 00:29:19,365
That's odd.

440
00:29:19,365 --> 00:29:21,833
When did fares get so high?

441
00:29:22,827 --> 00:29:24,703
Here.

442
00:29:24,703 --> 00:29:27,233
Thank you.

443
00:29:31,970 --> 00:29:33,016
Ma'am.

444
00:29:33,016 --> 00:29:34,449
Your change.

445
00:29:34,449 --> 00:29:35,506
Oh, right.

446
00:29:35,506 --> 00:29:37,557
My change.

447
00:29:38,710 --> 00:29:41,777
Mind waiting while I count the cash?

448
00:29:41,777 --> 00:29:43,048
I'll just count it.

449
00:29:43,048 --> 00:29:45,057
Won't take long.

450
00:29:45,057 --> 00:29:47,297
Just a moment.

451
00:29:48,941 --> 00:29:50,980
One,

452
00:29:50,980 --> 00:29:53,065
two,

453
00:29:53,065 --> 00:29:54,859
three,

454
00:29:54,859 --> 00:29:56,110
four,

455
00:29:56,110 --> 00:29:57,236
five,

456
00:29:57,236 --> 00:29:58,988
six,

457
00:29:58,988 --> 00:30:01,365
seven?

458
00:30:01,365 --> 00:30:04,201
I think you gave me an extra bill.

459
00:30:04,201 --> 00:30:06,912
Oh, you did that on purpose!

460
00:30:06,912 --> 00:30:09,707
Wow, what an angel!

461
00:30:09,707 --> 00:30:12,293
How'd he know I was broke?

462
00:30:12,293 --> 00:30:14,672
She's completely wasted.

463
00:30:36,177 --> 00:30:37,817
Oh, my...

464
00:30:39,054 --> 00:30:41,764
You must be exhausted.

465
00:30:43,991 --> 00:30:46,984
Want me to sing for you?

466
00:30:48,760 --> 00:30:52,666
- Don't...
- Singing gives me so much energy.

467
00:30:52,666 --> 00:30:57,042
It makes me feel better right here.

468
00:31:02,109 --> 00:31:09,799
♪ The sky is so beautiful ♪

469
00:31:10,976 --> 00:31:16,518
♪ Like a blue-violet dream ♪

470
00:31:17,900 --> 00:31:23,781
♪ The sky was on my side ♪

471
00:31:23,781 --> 00:31:27,159
♪ Will it happen again? ♪

472
00:31:27,159 --> 00:31:31,903
♪ I kept hoping for rain ♪

473
00:31:31,903 --> 00:31:35,751
♪ The truth is, I just wanted to see her ♪

474
00:31:35,751 --> 00:31:38,062
♪ My little... ♪

475
00:31:49,179 --> 00:31:51,574
Kwon Do Hyeok!

476
00:31:53,720 --> 00:31:55,525
Why are we here...

477
00:31:55,525 --> 00:31:57,716
Why is my wallet out here?

478
00:31:57,716 --> 00:31:58,732
What?

479
00:31:58,732 --> 00:32:01,134
Why is my bag here?

480
00:32:01,134 --> 00:32:03,237
What is going on?

481
00:32:03,237 --> 00:32:04,992
Kwon Do Hyeok, wake up!

482
00:32:04,992 --> 00:32:06,817
Kwon Do Hyeok!

483
00:32:07,575 --> 00:32:11,157
Is there anyone around?

484
00:32:11,157 --> 00:32:12,663
Wait, hold on.

485
00:32:12,663 --> 00:32:14,164
Hello?

486
00:32:14,164 --> 00:32:15,781
Wake up!

487
00:32:19,086 --> 00:32:20,597
Darn it.

488
00:32:20,597 --> 00:32:22,072
Hold on.

489
00:32:22,072 --> 00:32:24,508
Oh, no. 64 floors?

490
00:32:24,508 --> 00:32:26,260
I'll get motion sickness.

491
00:32:26,260 --> 00:32:28,847
What now? Keep going!

492
00:32:28,847 --> 00:32:30,213
Seriously...

493
00:32:33,606 --> 00:32:34,810
Go on in.

494
00:32:34,810 --> 00:32:36,963
You're so heavy!

495
00:32:41,303 --> 00:32:42,318
Jeez!

496
00:32:42,318 --> 00:32:43,747
Welcome home, boss.

497
00:32:43,747 --> 00:32:45,214
Oh, my!

498
00:32:46,498 --> 00:32:48,073
What?

499
00:32:48,073 --> 00:32:50,694
Even the greetings are automatic here.

500
00:32:51,980 --> 00:32:54,098
Why is this place so huge?

501
00:32:54,098 --> 00:32:56,866
All this space for one guy?

502
00:32:57,666 --> 00:32:58,792
Oh, there it is.

503
00:32:58,792 --> 00:33:00,013
Hold on.

504
00:33:00,869 --> 00:33:01,879
Come on.

505
00:33:01,879 --> 00:33:03,432
Almost there.

506
00:33:24,838 --> 00:33:27,487
What a lightweight.

507
00:33:33,905 --> 00:33:35,156
Wait.

508
00:33:36,808 --> 00:33:38,941
Off with this...

509
00:34:01,441 --> 00:34:04,812
He is handsome, though.

510
00:35:03,208 --> 00:35:06,448
This place has no personality.

511
00:35:06,920 --> 00:35:09,893
Not even a family photo.

512
00:35:09,893 --> 00:35:12,488
Not a graduation picture, either.

513
00:35:22,909 --> 00:35:25,609
What does this guy even eat?

514
00:35:55,719 --> 00:35:58,132
Did I sleep like this?

515
00:36:09,226 --> 00:36:11,606
How on earth...

516
00:36:16,673 --> 00:36:18,953
Lee Eun Chae...

517
00:37:03,654 --> 00:37:05,353
So warm...

518
00:37:05,353 --> 00:37:07,540
Nice and warm.

519
00:37:15,549 --> 00:37:17,389
Oh, crap.

520
00:37:19,386 --> 00:37:20,955
What the...

521
00:37:21,425 --> 00:37:23,217
I'm screwed.

522
00:37:26,607 --> 00:37:28,328
I'm going to puke.

523
00:37:45,913 --> 00:37:47,359
I feel sick...

524
00:38:00,863 --> 00:38:03,862
What are those muscles?

525
00:38:05,262 --> 00:38:08,448
He's sculpted like a statue.

526
00:39:24,511 --> 00:39:26,691
Coffee's on its way, boss.

527
00:39:34,185 --> 00:39:36,887
She must be out of her mind.

528
00:39:36,887 --> 00:39:37,927
[Dad]

529
00:39:46,575 --> 00:39:47,951
Hey, you little...

530
00:39:47,951 --> 00:39:49,877
While I'm still alive and kicking,

531
00:39:49,877 --> 00:39:50,991
you were out all night?

532
00:39:50,991 --> 00:39:53,504
I'll shave your head!

533
00:39:54,332 --> 00:39:55,834
Hello?

534
00:39:55,834 --> 00:39:57,002
Hello...

535
00:39:57,002 --> 00:39:58,053
Hey...

536
00:40:04,760 --> 00:40:07,846
What happens if you break curfew?

537
00:40:07,846 --> 00:40:09,099
He'll shave my head.

538
00:40:09,806 --> 00:40:11,751
Was she serious?

539
00:40:12,267 --> 00:40:15,740
She's already a mess.
What if he shaves her head?

540
00:40:16,294 --> 00:40:18,094
Oh, man...

541
00:40:25,582 --> 00:40:28,476
No shoes, no wallet...

542
00:40:29,284 --> 00:40:31,643
I left my phone, too!

543
00:40:32,579 --> 00:40:36,145
How am I supposed to get home like this?

544
00:40:39,252 --> 00:40:42,545
"I just happened to catch a glimpse."

545
00:40:43,799 --> 00:40:45,285
Should I go with that?

546
00:40:52,557 --> 00:40:55,103
I stood there staring like an idiot.

547
00:40:55,103 --> 00:40:56,795
I mean, who showers

548
00:40:56,795 --> 00:40:59,523
without even locking the door?

549
00:40:59,523 --> 00:41:02,696
Then again, it's his place. Why would he?

550
00:41:02,696 --> 00:41:05,205
I'm the one who messed up.

551
00:41:10,698 --> 00:41:12,223
I don't know.

552
00:41:12,932 --> 00:41:14,443
Whatever.

553
00:41:17,260 --> 00:41:20,024
Boss, that woman's back.

554
00:41:43,379 --> 00:41:46,267
I didn't see a thing.

555
00:41:46,778 --> 00:41:49,329
You're a terrible liar.

556
00:41:50,048 --> 00:41:52,301
I've never been the only one naked.

557
00:41:52,301 --> 00:41:53,618
What does that mean...

558
00:41:53,618 --> 00:41:54,744
Gosh!

559
00:41:54,744 --> 00:41:57,831
Does he want to see me naked, too?

560
00:41:57,831 --> 00:42:01,001
Not like you to get so flustered.

561
00:42:01,001 --> 00:42:04,431
Could this be your first time?

562
00:42:05,057 --> 00:42:07,048
No!

563
00:42:07,048 --> 00:42:09,081
I've seen plenty!

564
00:42:10,218 --> 00:42:11,845
My first time? Please.

565
00:42:11,845 --> 00:42:14,848
I can't believe I'm even telling you this,

566
00:42:14,848 --> 00:42:16,922
but the number of guys

567
00:42:16,922 --> 00:42:19,936
who've shown me theirs could fill a truck!

568
00:42:19,936 --> 00:42:23,940
And they all looked way better than you!

569
00:42:23,940 --> 00:42:26,975
- Their skin was...
- Then show me yours.

570
00:42:28,782 --> 00:42:31,087
Stay back!

571
00:42:31,885 --> 00:42:33,760
You...

572
00:42:33,760 --> 00:42:35,909
You're a sex addict. Right?

573
00:42:36,578 --> 00:42:38,855
What are you talking about?

574
00:42:39,664 --> 00:42:43,712
I meant, prove you've got that much experience.

575
00:42:44,407 --> 00:42:46,057
Darn it.

576
00:42:54,596 --> 00:42:58,725
If that's an act, she deserves an Oscar.

577
00:43:00,477 --> 00:43:02,196
Unbelievable.

578
00:43:03,939 --> 00:43:06,779
I'll shave your head!

579
00:43:10,670 --> 00:43:12,405
I'll drive you.

580
00:43:12,405 --> 00:43:16,136
- No, thanks!
- It's for my own peace of mind.

581
00:43:17,744 --> 00:43:18,921
But...

582
00:43:22,958 --> 00:43:26,351
Does he really think I'll fall for that?

583
00:43:28,206 --> 00:43:31,311
Still, saves me taxi fare.

584
00:43:35,804 --> 00:43:40,308
If the elevator breaks or there's a blackout,

585
00:43:40,308 --> 00:43:43,325
do you have to climb 64 floors?

586
00:43:43,325 --> 00:43:46,276
I've never met anyone who worries about that.

587
00:43:46,276 --> 00:43:48,942
You never know what could happen.

588
00:43:48,942 --> 00:43:52,396
No matter what happens,
you come when your boss calls.

589
00:43:52,396 --> 00:43:53,430
No way.

590
00:43:53,430 --> 00:43:55,773
I'd never make it up all those stairs.

591
00:43:55,773 --> 00:43:58,951
So you'd leave your boss trapped up here?

592
00:43:58,951 --> 00:44:01,371
Your own fault. For living this high up.

593
00:44:01,371 --> 00:44:04,849
It's called success, not my own fault.

594
00:44:04,849 --> 00:44:06,835
Success or not,

595
00:44:06,835 --> 00:44:09,735
I'm not climbing all the way up here.

596
00:44:12,757 --> 00:44:18,224
If I ever walked up 64 floors,

597
00:44:18,224 --> 00:44:21,683
it'd take the power of love.

598
00:44:21,683 --> 00:44:23,233
"Love?"

599
00:44:25,685 --> 00:44:27,093
Well...

600
00:44:27,658 --> 00:44:30,345
That would never happen.

601
00:44:39,983 --> 00:44:41,821
Are you getting in?

602
00:44:41,821 --> 00:44:44,229
The power of love?

603
00:44:52,617 --> 00:44:55,340
Feels like a free-fall ride.

604
00:44:58,504 --> 00:45:00,430
If I ever came all this way for you,

605
00:45:00,430 --> 00:45:03,738
it'd take the power of love.

606
00:45:22,744 --> 00:45:25,542
Maybe I should play some music.

607
00:45:30,752 --> 00:45:33,129
Too loud. Turn it off.

608
00:45:33,129 --> 00:45:35,835
It's too quiet without it...

609
00:46:01,799 --> 00:46:05,620
You don't seem worried
about getting caught staying out.

610
00:46:05,620 --> 00:46:10,566
It's called mind over matter.

611
00:46:26,910 --> 00:46:28,343
I'm off.

612
00:46:32,689 --> 00:46:34,441
He must be asleep.

613
00:46:34,441 --> 00:46:35,808
Okay.

614
00:46:36,329 --> 00:46:37,828
Goodbye!

615
00:47:29,787 --> 00:47:31,206
Back?

616
00:47:31,206 --> 00:47:32,528
Dad!

617
00:47:34,334 --> 00:47:35,710
Oh, my God!

618
00:47:35,710 --> 00:47:38,087
Dad! No way... Are you serious?

619
00:47:38,087 --> 00:47:39,518
- Oh, no!
- Get over here!

620
00:47:39,518 --> 00:47:40,478
Calm down, Dad!

621
00:47:40,478 --> 00:47:41,674
- How dare...
- Please!

622
00:47:41,674 --> 00:47:42,807
- Sorry!
- Get over here!

623
00:47:55,362 --> 00:47:56,397
Drive!

624
00:47:56,397 --> 00:47:58,316
Why? What's going on?

625
00:47:58,316 --> 00:48:00,438
Dad's chasing me with hair clippers!

626
00:48:00,438 --> 00:48:02,487
He really was going to shave your head?

627
00:48:02,487 --> 00:48:04,860
Come on! Drive already!

628
00:48:04,860 --> 00:48:06,241
Put your seat belt on!

629
00:48:06,241 --> 00:48:08,046
Okay, okay!

630
00:48:17,710 --> 00:48:19,508
Where to?

631
00:48:22,067 --> 00:48:24,028
Where am I driving?

632
00:48:36,980 --> 00:48:40,233
We need to head to work anyway...

633
00:48:40,233 --> 00:48:42,486
Let's get breakfast first.

634
00:48:45,579 --> 00:48:49,279
[Seoul Grandma's Beef Head Soup]

635
00:48:58,615 --> 00:49:01,216
[Seoul Grandma's Beef Head Soup]

636
00:49:09,307 --> 00:49:10,847
Careful, it's hot.

637
00:49:10,847 --> 00:49:12,632
Thank you.

638
00:49:12,632 --> 00:49:14,578
Oh, that looks good.

639
00:49:17,353 --> 00:49:18,479
Enjoy your meal.

640
00:49:18,479 --> 00:49:20,732
Thank you.

641
00:49:20,732 --> 00:49:22,679
Now, like this...

642
00:49:22,679 --> 00:49:25,700
Add a good scoop of rice...

643
00:49:27,697 --> 00:49:29,008
So...

644
00:49:29,008 --> 00:49:30,437
Cow's head, huh?

645
00:49:31,239 --> 00:49:33,852
They make the broth from beef head,

646
00:49:33,852 --> 00:49:35,538
then add the meat,

647
00:49:35,538 --> 00:49:36,998
with chopped scallions...

648
00:49:36,998 --> 00:49:38,632
Enough.

649
00:49:41,044 --> 00:49:42,712
Try it.

650
00:49:42,712 --> 00:49:44,047
It's good for you.

651
00:49:44,047 --> 00:49:46,250
My body's fine as it is.

652
00:49:46,883 --> 00:49:49,843
You have to add all the good stuff.

653
00:49:52,805 --> 00:49:55,956
Your fridge was completely empty.

654
00:49:55,956 --> 00:49:57,830
Don't you eat at home?

655
00:49:57,830 --> 00:50:00,084
No, I don't.

656
00:50:00,084 --> 00:50:01,814
Then...

657
00:50:01,814 --> 00:50:04,703
What do you have when you're hungry?

658
00:50:05,276 --> 00:50:06,277
Wine...

659
00:50:06,277 --> 00:50:09,072
and water?

660
00:50:09,072 --> 00:50:11,896
Wait, so...

661
00:50:11,896 --> 00:50:13,776
Do you just never get hungry?

662
00:50:13,776 --> 00:50:17,274
Eating meals on a fixed schedule...

663
00:50:17,274 --> 00:50:19,290
Isn't that a waste of time?

664
00:50:19,290 --> 00:50:20,934
So...

665
00:50:22,021 --> 00:50:24,547
You only have a sex drive, huh?

666
00:50:34,097 --> 00:50:35,657
Have you ever heard

667
00:50:35,657 --> 00:50:39,397
the saying "food gives you strength?"

668
00:50:39,397 --> 00:50:42,206
But I think it's not just the body.

669
00:50:42,206 --> 00:50:44,575
Food feeds the heart, too.

670
00:50:44,575 --> 00:50:48,820
Sitting down face-to-face,
and sharing a meal...

671
00:50:48,820 --> 00:50:51,366
That's something special.

672
00:50:58,765 --> 00:51:01,118
So go on, try it.

673
00:51:02,041 --> 00:51:04,377
I have to do everything for you?

674
00:51:04,377 --> 00:51:08,015
If I use my own spoon,
you'll complain it's gross again.

675
00:51:08,015 --> 00:51:10,881
Yeah... Like this.

676
00:51:10,881 --> 00:51:12,450
Eat up.

677
00:51:15,366 --> 00:51:17,357
You'll be amazed.

678
00:51:26,759 --> 00:51:28,396
Good, right?

679
00:51:30,486 --> 00:51:32,492
Surprised?

680
00:51:37,869 --> 00:51:39,443
Look at you.

681
00:51:48,659 --> 00:51:50,995
I'm stuffed.

682
00:51:56,304 --> 00:51:57,464
Jin Woo.

683
00:51:58,144 --> 00:52:00,016
Where are you now?

684
00:52:00,016 --> 00:52:01,915
We've all been worried sick.

685
00:52:01,915 --> 00:52:04,121
We had a work dinner,
so I crashed at the office.

686
00:52:04,121 --> 00:52:05,548
Don't worry.

687
00:52:05,548 --> 00:52:07,273
How can we not worry?

688
00:52:07,273 --> 00:52:10,109
It's dangerous out there.

689
00:52:10,109 --> 00:52:12,796
Especially for a pretty girl like you.

690
00:52:12,796 --> 00:52:17,280
True. There are so many creeps out there.

691
00:52:18,367 --> 00:52:21,187
That's why your dad was worried.

692
00:52:21,768 --> 00:52:27,376
I'm at work now, so please talk to Dad for me.

693
00:52:27,376 --> 00:52:28,788
Okay.

694
00:52:29,879 --> 00:52:31,714
"Work?"

695
00:52:31,714 --> 00:52:34,384
You're quite the liar.

696
00:52:34,384 --> 00:52:38,721
I can't tell him I slept at your place, can I?

697
00:52:38,721 --> 00:52:42,714
You're making it sound like
something happened between us.

698
00:52:47,227 --> 00:52:48,272
Aren't you getting in?

699
00:52:48,272 --> 00:52:49,857
Forget it.

700
00:52:49,857 --> 00:52:53,537
People will really think
something happened between us.

701
00:52:53,537 --> 00:52:54,565
Why?

702
00:52:54,565 --> 00:52:56,989
You said nothing happened.

703
00:52:56,989 --> 00:52:59,415
Who cares what people think?

704
00:53:17,394 --> 00:53:18,427
What?

705
00:53:18,427 --> 00:53:20,127
They came together?

706
00:53:29,814 --> 00:53:34,110
For New OX's new album, we went with fiery red.

707
00:53:34,110 --> 00:53:37,363
The performance will be bold, too.

708
00:53:37,363 --> 00:53:39,168
Nice work.

709
00:53:40,376 --> 00:53:42,785
Music isn't about genre.

710
00:53:42,785 --> 00:53:45,098
It's about the world an artist creates.

711
00:53:45,098 --> 00:53:48,958
Whether it's a song or an instrumental.

712
00:53:48,958 --> 00:53:50,456
But...

713
00:53:50,456 --> 00:53:54,344
What kind of world has New OX built?

714
00:53:55,818 --> 00:53:57,473
What world?

715
00:53:57,473 --> 00:53:58,972
Do you know?

716
00:53:58,972 --> 00:54:00,178
What?

717
00:54:01,971 --> 00:54:04,217
You said I know nothing about idols, huh?

718
00:54:04,217 --> 00:54:05,818
Yes.

719
00:54:05,818 --> 00:54:07,938
And you're right.

720
00:54:07,938 --> 00:54:11,675
Then even someone like me
should buy into their world

721
00:54:11,675 --> 00:54:14,283
and feel something.

722
00:54:14,283 --> 00:54:15,372
Right?

723
00:54:15,372 --> 00:54:18,372
Shouldn't they have a universe like that?

724
00:54:25,107 --> 00:54:26,593
Well...

725
00:54:33,811 --> 00:54:35,922
What are we, novelists?

726
00:54:35,922 --> 00:54:38,049
What's with all this universe talk?

727
00:54:38,049 --> 00:54:39,859
Isn't that a video game thing?

728
00:54:39,859 --> 00:54:41,497
No, that's not it.

729
00:54:54,899 --> 00:54:58,295
You spent the ten million already?

730
00:54:58,295 --> 00:55:00,812
Oh, that?

731
00:55:00,812 --> 00:55:05,743
I threw it in that sleazy manager's face!

732
00:55:05,743 --> 00:55:07,853
Take this and get lost!

733
00:55:07,853 --> 00:55:11,607
You two-bit creep!

734
00:55:16,504 --> 00:55:17,546
Yes, sir.

735
00:55:17,546 --> 00:55:19,202
Come in for a moment.

736
00:55:27,740 --> 00:55:32,353
Find out what happened to Eun Chae
at her previous job.

737
00:55:32,353 --> 00:55:34,381
Lee Eun Chae?

738
00:55:34,381 --> 00:55:35,849
Yes.

739
00:55:40,736 --> 00:55:42,161
Understood.

740
00:56:52,842 --> 00:56:56,020
I need data on the kind of men women fall for.

741
00:56:56,020 --> 00:56:57,867
She looks smitten already.

742
00:56:57,867 --> 00:56:59,315
Don't try to bait me like this.

743
00:56:59,315 --> 00:57:00,941
It only makes me dislike you more.

744
00:57:00,941 --> 00:57:02,276
Why do you need money?

745
00:57:02,276 --> 00:57:04,904
Because I owe a dangerous rich heir money.

746
00:57:04,904 --> 00:57:06,387
Eun Chae, do you want a blind date?

747
00:57:06,387 --> 00:57:09,389
Why does she get under my skin?

748
00:57:09,389 --> 00:57:12,078
Next show, I'll buy them myself.

749
00:57:12,078 --> 00:57:13,746
Fine! I'm Soo!

750
00:57:13,746 --> 00:57:15,369
How about living together for three days?

751
00:57:15,369 --> 00:57:17,046
You really came?

752
00:57:17,046 --> 00:57:18,953
Then can I kiss you?
